      "source": [
        "### Dataset 2: Visitation Data EDA\n",
        "\n",
        "This section explores Dataset #2 — Yoesmite Visitation Data for (1979–2025). We load the fully wrangled dataset directly from data/02-processed/yosemite_visitor_cleaned.csv. The goal is to understand typical visitation patterns and identify variance within each month.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Distribution of Monthly Visitorship\n",
        "\n",
        "The plot below shows the distribution of visitors per month. This gives us a visual way to understand a common number of visitors as the seasons progress. We can see an increase in visitorship during the warmer seasons, and we can also see an increase in variance in these seasons. Warmer seasons increase fire risk, which in turn increase average AQI. Thus, this supports the idea that visitorship may fluctuate negatively due to an increase in AQI."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import statsmodels.api as sm\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "\n",
        "#import data\n",
        "df = pd.read_csv(('data/02-processed/yosemite_visitors_cleaned.csv'), index_col='Date', parse_dates=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "df['Month'] = df.index.month_name()\n",
        "\n",
        "#plot data\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
        "sns.boxplot(x='Month', y='Visitors', data=df,\n",
        "            order=['January', 'February', 'March', 'April', 'May', 'June',\n",
        "                   'July', 'August', 'September', 'October', 'November', 'December'])\n",
        "plt.title('Distribution of Visitors by Month (1979-2025)')\n",
        "plt.xticks(rotation=45)\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "#---------------\n",
        "# Load and prepare data\n",
        "df = pd.read_csv('data/02-processed/yosemite_visitors_cleaned.csv')\n",
        "df['Date'] = pd.to_datetime(df['Date'])\n",
        "df = df.sort_values('Date').set_index('Date')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Global Variance and Distribution Stats\n",
        "global_stats = df['Visitors'].agg(['mean', 'median', 'var', 'std', 'skew'])\n",
        "\n",
        "# Monthly Volatility, Grouping by month to see seasonal variance\n",
        "# Coeff of var CV = std / mean\n",
        "monthly_stats = df.groupby(df.index.month_name())['Visitors'].agg(['mean', 'var', 'std'])\n",
        "monthly_stats['CV'] = monthly_stats['std'] / monthly_stats['mean']\n",
        "\n",
        "# 3.variation by decade\n",
        "df['Decade'] = (df.index.year // 10) * 10\n",
        "decade_stats = df.groupby('Decade')['Visitors'].agg(['mean', 'var', 'std'])\n",
        "decade_stats['CV'] = decade_stats['std'] / decade_stats['mean']\n",
        "\n",
        "# 4.YoY % Change\n",
        "annual_totals = df['Visitors'].resample('A').sum()\n",
        "yoy_growth = annual_totals.pct_change()\n",
        "growth_variance = yoy_growth.var()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Display Results\n",
        "print(\"Global Summary Statistics:\")\n",
        "print(global_stats)\n",
        "print(\"\\nMonthly Volatility (Sorted by CV):\")\n",
        "print(monthly_stats.sort_values('CV', ascending=False))"
      ],
